Add performance tracking, limit orders, and MA crossover trading bot

Features:
- Performance tracking: PortfolioSnapshot and PerformanceTracker record
  equity history and compute daily return, total value, overall growth
  %, and profit/loss. Exposed through a new Performance tab.
- Limit orders and stop losses: PendingOrder models LIMIT_BUY,
  LIMIT_SELL, and STOP_LOSS triggers. OrderMonitorService runs a daemon
  ScheduledExecutorService that polls prices and executes triggered
  orders off the EDT, dispatching GUI updates via invokeLater. Exposed
  through a new Orders tab.
- Trading bot and backtesting: PriceBar and MovingAverageCrossoverBot
  implement an SMA crossover strategy for both live paper trading and
  historical backtesting, with trade log, win rate, and P&L reporting.
  Backtest runs on a SwingWorker. Exposed through a new Bot tab.

Refactoring:
- Portfolio: add estimateHoldingsValue() for snapshot valuation.
- StockMarketGUI: replace single layout with JTabbedPane hosting the
  Trading, Performance, Orders, and Bot tabs; stop the order monitor
  on window close.

Cleanup (resolves IDE warnings):
- Remove unused imports across LoginWindow, RegisterWindow,
  StockMarketGUI.
- Make fields final where assigned once (LoginWindow, RegisterWindow,
  Stock, StockMarketGUI).
- Remove unused Stock.stocks field.
- Remove unused entryPrice field from MovingAverageCrossoverBot.
- Fix unused local variable in PerformanceTracker.profitAndLoss().
- Remove unused serialVersionUID from StockMarketGUI.
